      year: "1962",
      title: "Eastern Gopuram, Sri Anjaneya Temple",
      place: "Karaikudi, Sivaganga District",
      kind: "Repainting & polychrome restoration",
      note: "Six-tala eastern gopuram repainted in mineral pigments over a fresh lime-and-jaggery ground. Original 19th-century stucco figures consolidated, not recarved. The vermilion of the kumbha-panjara band was matched to surviving traces under the cornice.",
      master: "Stapathi V. Ramaswamy (founder)",
      materials: "Lime mortar, jaggery, kadukkai decoction, mineral vermilion, peacock-blue indigo, gold leaf on kalashas"
